      <div type="clause" n="6.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 6.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="288" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ ealle Godes þeowas we biddað ⁊ lærað ⁊ huruþinga sacerdas, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#ICn_6-1.lnote.oe.15"/> Gode hyran ⁊ clænnesse lufian ⁊ beorgan heom sylfu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> wið Godes yrre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#ICn_6-1.lnote.oe.16"/> ⁊ wið ðone weallendan brýne, þe weallað<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#ICn_6-1.lnote.oe.17"/> on helle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="288" ed="#liebermann"/>Ænd<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_6-1.lnote.oe.2-2"/> ealle Godes þeowas we byddað ⁊ lærað ⁊ huruþinga sacerdas, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hig Gode hira<hi rend="italic">n</hi> ⁊ clænnissa lufian ⁊ beorgum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_6-1.lnote.oe.5"/> heom sylfum wið Godes irre ⁊ wið þonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_6-1.lnote.oe.6"/> weallendan bryne, þe wealleð on helle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="6.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="288" ed="#liebermann"/>et ei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#ICn_6-1.lnote.oe.11"/> digne seruiant et castitatem diligant,</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6.1" corresp="#wit-d-frags"><pb n="289" ed="#liebermann"/>And ealle Godes þeowas we biddað ⁊ lǽrað ⁊ huruþinga sacerdas, ⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†" target="#ICn_6-1.lnote.oe.dagger"/> hi Gode hiran ⁊ clænnesse lufian ⁊ beorgan hi<hi rend="italic">m</hi> silfu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> wið Godes irre ⁊ wið ðone weallendan bryne, þe wealleð on helle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="6.1" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="289" ed="#liebermann"/>castitatem seruent, ab ira<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#ICn_6-1.lnote.oe.17-2"/> Dei sibi caueant et alios uiuendo et monendo castigent, ut se ab infernali incendio custodiant.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="6.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="289" ed="#liebermann"/>Omnes namque Dei ministros precamur et monemus, et maxime sacerdotes, ut Deo obediant et castitatem diligant, semetipsos tuentes ab ira Dei [et] feruenti incendio quod feruet in inferno.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="6a.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="162" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ ealle Godes þeowas we biddað ⁊ lærað ⁊ huruþinga sacerdas, þæt hi Gode hyran ⁊ clænnesse lufian ⁊ beorgan heom sylfum wið Godes yrre ⁊ wið ðone weallendan brýne þe weallað on helle.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="240" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And ealle Godes þeowas we biddað and lærað, and huruþinga sacerdas, þæt hi Gode hyran and clænnesse lufian and beorgan heom sylfum wið Godes yrre and wið ðone weallendan bryne, þe weallað on helle.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="289" ed="#liebermann"/>Und alle Gottesdiener bitten und weisen wir an, und vor allen Dingen Priester, dass sie Gott gehorchen und Keuschheit pflegen und sich selbst vor Gottes Zorne hüten und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_6-1.lnote.de.1"/> vor dem wallenden Feuer, das wallt in der Hölle.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And we ask and instruct all servants of God, and above all priests, to obey God and love chastity, and guard themselves against God's anger and against the surging fire that surges in hell.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_6-1.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="163" ed="#robertson"/>And we pray and enjoin all the servants of God, and priests above all, to obey God and practice celibacy and guard themselves<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#ICn_6-1.robnote.n.2"/> from the wrath of God and from the raging fire which blazes in hell<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#ICn_6-1.robnote.n.3"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="241" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And we require and instruct that all servants of God, especially priests, obey God, embrace celibacy, and protect themselves against God’s wrath and against the burning fire that rages in hell.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="289"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_5">VI Atr 5</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. VI Atr. 5</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_5">VI Atr 5–5.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 6:1-2a: Cn 1018 11:1-2  VI Atr 5-5:1, 5:3</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_5-3">VI Atr 5.3</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 6:1-2a: Cn 1018 11:1-2  VI Atr 5-5:1, 5:3</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-022">Cn 1018 11.1–2</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 6:1-2a: Cn 1018 11:1-2  VI Atr 5-5:1, 5:3</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="334"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_41">VI Atr 41</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">A's ‘beorgum’ should be corrected to ‘beorgan’. D's ‘⁊ hi’ should be ‘þæt hi’. Liebermann compares VI Atr 5.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 289, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_6-1.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">288</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hig God hiran ⁊ clænnisse l. ⁊ beorgum [<hi rend="italic">vgl. A</hi>] <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hig God hiran ⁊ clænnisse l. ⁊ beorgum [cf. A] Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_6-1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">288</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">irre <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">irre Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_6-1.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">288</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-leþ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-leþ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_6-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">288</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">assidue <hi rend="italic">fügt hier zu K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">assidue added here by K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_6-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">289</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">omitted</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_6-1.lnote.oe.dagger" n="†" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">289</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> þæt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read þæt</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_6-1.lnote.oe.17-2" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">289</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">D. i. <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">D. i. Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_6-1.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">288</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_6-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">288</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> beorgan</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read beorgan</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_6-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">288</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl. o.</hi> 3<hi rend="italic">a</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. above 3a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_6-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">199</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">In denselben Worten nochmals II 84, 3; mit der Hölle (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 3) droht auch I 7. 7, 3. 18b. 25. Hieraus <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 269</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">In the same words again II 84, 3; hell (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 3) is also threatened in I 7. 7, 3. 18b. 25. Hence <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 269</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_6-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. VI Atr. 5; Wulfstan, p. 269</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_6-1.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. II Cn. 84, 3.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_6-1.robnote.n.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. caps. 7, 3; 18 <hi rend="italic">b</hi>; 25, also IV Edg. 1, 4; VI Atr. 12, 1.</seg></note>
